    "done_when": "Shared interface between the mesh and the tree (both nodes build to it): the mesh returns a frozen dataclass ContourMesh in nova/equilibrium/contour_tree_mesh.py with fixed-capacity jax arrays vertex_rz (V,2) m, vertex_psi (V,) Wb, vertex_valid (V,) bool, vertex_is_wall (V,) bool, edges (E,2) int32 vertex indices, edge_valid (E,) bool, triangles (T,3) int32, triangle_valid (T,) bool, plus the capacities V, E, T and an overflow flag; the tree consumes vertex_psi, vertex_valid, vertex_is_wall, edges and edge_valid only, and sigma from contour_tree.sigma_for_state. Read the plan's section 2 at main (clarified tonight: the triangulation is clipped to the vessel polygon, flux is valued at the hex-cell centres, and wall-vertex flux is interpolated linearly on the containing triangle of the same piecewise-linear field, with no smooth field). In the new module nova/equilibrium/contour_tree_mesh.py, build ContourMesh from hex cell centres, their psi and the multi-unit wall. Reuse StencilMesh's Delaunay neighbour rings and the multi-unit polygon containment named in docs/evidence/contour-tree-topology-authority/reuse-map.md rows 1 to 3 rather than writing new ones, and say in the module which you reused. Triangles are the three-direction mesh of adjacent hex centres; triangles are clipped to the vessel polygon; wall vertices are added where triangle edges cross the wall polyline, and each takes its psi by linear interpolation on its containing triangle. tests/test_contour_tree_mesh.py asserts: (a) on a synthetic linear field psi = a*R + b*Z + c every wall vertex's interpolated psi equals the analytic value to 1e-12 Wb (negative control: nearest-centre valuation fails it, logged); (b) every valid vertex lies inside or on the vessel polygon, and replacing the polygon by its bounding box admits vertices that the polygon excludes (control); (c) Euler characteristic V - E + T = 1 for a simply connected clipped domain; (d) an over-capacity input sets the overflow flag; (e) the build is jit-traceable at fixed capacity. Run in a fresh process in place (TMPDIR=/tmp, JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu, configure_dtypes before any array). Logs under docs/figures/contour-tree-topology-authority/mesh/ (force-add).",
